# section s56
# A pan, not a scroll, and this is the one place in the flow that needs it.
#
# `scroll --pixels` is a flick: the number is a gesture magnitude and momentum
# carries it much further -- measured on this runner, 60pt of gesture moved the
# list 434pt. The ALERTS heading is 13pt tall, so no flick magnitude lands on
# it; every one of them carries the heading from below the viewport to above it
# between two visibility checks. 320 and 120 were both tried and both overshot
# to the same place, with `Haptic feedback` at y=16 and the heading just off the
# top.
#
# It used to pass only because the page ended soon after ALERTS, so the flick
# hit the bottom stop and settled there. Adding the brand mark and version to
# the foot gave the list room to keep travelling, and the accident stopped
# working.
#
# `gesture pan <x> <y> <dx> <dy> <ms>` moves the distance it is given. 120pt per
# iteration cannot skip a 13pt heading, and the step's own 20s timeout has room
# for the extra iterations.
gesture pan 200 600 0 -120 400

# section s57
# A pan for the same reason `s56` uses one: these three targets sit within a
# couple of rows of each other, and a flick's momentum carries whichever one is
# sought clear past the top of the screen. When that happens the row's centre
# lands in the status bar, and pressing there is not a miss -- iOS reads a
# status-bar tap as "scroll to top", so the list jumps home and the control was
# never touched. A press that reported success at (339, 36) is what that looks
# like from the runner's side.
gesture pan 200 600 0 -120 400

# section s58
scroll down --pixels 160 --duration-ms 300
wait stable 300 5000

# section scroll-notifications
# A pan for the same reason `s56` uses one: these three targets sit within a
# couple of rows of each other, and a flick's momentum carries whichever one is
# sought clear past the top of the screen. When that happens the row's centre
# lands in the status bar, and pressing there is not a miss -- iOS reads a
# status-bar tap as "scroll to top", so the list jumps home and the control was
# never touched. A press that reported success at (339, 36) is what that looks
# like from the runner's side.
gesture pan 200 600 0 -120 400

